# Copy this file to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in your own values.
# Vite inlines anything prefixed with VITE_ into the bundle, so never put a
# secret in here.

# Google Maps JavaScript API
# --------------------------
# The dashboard renders a real Google Map of the campus.
#
# Fastest path, no billing required (prototyping only): get a Maps Demo Key at
#   https://console.cloud.google.com/google/maps-hosted/tos
# and paste it below. It covers map rendering, markers and info windows — all
# this dashboard uses — with a daily quota and no risk of charges. It expects
# `DEMO_MAP_ID`, which is the app's fallback when VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID is
# unset, so no Map ID is needed alongside it.
#
# For production, use a standard key instead:
#   1. Pick (or create) a Google Cloud project and enable billing on it.
#   2. Enable "Maps JavaScript API" for that project.
#   3. Create an API key under APIs & Services > Credentials. Restrict it to the
#      Maps JavaScript API, and to the origins you serve the app from
#      (http://localhost:5173 for `npm run dev`).
#   4. Paste the key below.
#
# Without a key the map area shows a styled setup notice instead of a map.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Optional Google Maps Map ID (Maps > Map Management in the Cloud console).
# Advanced markers — the numbered bin markers — require a map ID, and a Map ID
# is also what enables Cloud-based map styling. When this is empty the app uses
# Google's documented `DEMO_MAP_ID`, which is fine for local development but
# must not be used in production.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID=

# Campus API
# ----------
# Base URL of the Express backend (`backend/`, default port 5000). The map
# reads the live `bins` collection through `GET /api/bins` and signs in through
# `POST /api/auth/login`, so the backend must be running for real data.
# Leave this unset for local development.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
